	The Loadout wing (Terra) archway on the plaza's west wall: a cracked stone arch with rough stacked-boulder
	pillars, crystal clusters flanking the emblem and bursting from the north pillar, a crystal vein in the long
	crack of each side (crown -> floor), and a pebble trickle.  36 pieces, 4410 triangles.
	Units / conventions:
	  * All numbers are integers in THOUSANDTHS of a stud, Roblox WORLD axes (x, y, z), comma-joined in strings.
	  * Piece C = centre of the piece's box (world); V = its unique vertices relative to C; T = triangles,
	    0-based indices into V, counter-clockwise seen from outside (single-sided MeshParts show the outside).
	    Vertices are shared between triangles: give every triangle its own face normal (flat / faceted look).
	  * Classes give each piece its Color (hex) + Material.  Neon classes: Crystal, Vein, Stripe.
	  * Vein_01..Vein_12: the vein in path order, crown (01) -> floor (12); each segment holds the same stretch
	    of BOTH sides (south + north), so a pulse travelling 01 -> 12 runs down both pillars together.
	    Vein.Period = seconds for one pulse to travel the whole path.
	  * Stripe_*: exact copy of the two floor-stripe pieces of OBS_El_Terra_01 (which is hidden whole).
	  * Hide: hub MeshParts to hide locally at this archway.  Lights: PointLights (At = world position).
	  * Pebbles: V/T = one small pebble mesh relative to its own centre; Sources = world points (crack mouths on
	    the pillars) to drop pebbles from -- the straight drop line below each is clear of the arch;
	    Floor = world y (studs) the pebbles bounce on.  ]]
